    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "IE (native valve), oxacillin-resistant staphylococci: vancomycin 15 mg/kg IV q12h alone × 6 wk. Penicillin-allergic, streptococci: vancomycin 15 mg/kg IV q12h × 4 wk (NVE; 6 wk for PVE)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Invasive MRSA:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " dose to an AUC of 400–600 (trough targeting no longer recommended). Monitor renal function in all patients."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Main ADR is hypersensitivity. Infusion reaction (histamine-mediated pruritus/flushing of face, neck, shoulders) if infused too fast. AKI rises with exposure and with other nephrotoxins (eg, aminoglycosides; possibly pip-tazo). Reversible neutropenia/thrombocytopenia; dose-related ototoxicity unusual (more with other ototoxic drugs)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Prior allergic reaction to vancomycin. Pregnancy: IV only if clearly needed (oral is fine for C. difficile)."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
